## What They Do

Black Aegis Private Limited (founder: Sanket Nadagouda) has submitted a proposal to DISC 14 Problem Statement 69 (Indian Air Force) for a Secure Information Exchange Platform for Military Units (SIEPMU) over public internet — branded as CyberMesh SIEPMU.

**Core architecture:** Distributed trust model combining sender-side encryption, recipient-side decryption, zero-trust verification at every hop, quorum-governed key recovery (Shamir Secret Sharing, 3-of-5 model), 14-engine metadata-bounded threat detection, role-based and relationship-aware access control, and an adapter-based integration layer for designated IAF systems.

**Key technical differentiators:** No single trust point — trust distributed across identity, policy, key governance, monitoring, and audit services. Relay nodes handle encrypted transport only; they are not content-trust points. Quorum key recovery requires organisational and geographic separation, dual-authorisation, and logged reconstruction events.

**Proposed timeline:** 9 months across 3 phases — platform integration (Months 1–3), detection layer and key control (Months 4–6), representative deployment and handover (Months 7–9).

**iDEX mechanism:** DISC 14 SPARK Grant Agreement; milestone-based funding release.

